const title = 'The Bountiful Keyboard · What an API is, and why builders with agents should care';
const description =
  'Start here: what an API is, why it is the most interesting idea on the internet right now, and what grows when anyone with an AI agent can build on one. With live labs that call the PointCast Keyboard API. By Michael Hoydich.';

const agentPromptBase = `You are helping me build a small web page that uses the PointCast Keyboard API.

The API (open, no key, CORS *):
- POST https://pointcast.xyz/api/keyboard/signal
  JSON body: { "notes": [MIDI numbers 0-127, up to 64], "app": "my-app-name" }
  or { "count": 1-200 } for unpitched keystrokes. Never send text.
  Reply: { "ok": true, "globalTotal": n, "id": n }
- GET https://pointcast.xyz/api/keyboard/signal
  Reply: totals, sources, today's key (key.today), recent phrases
- GET https://pointcast.xyz/api/keyboard/signal?since=<id>
  Reply: { latestId, phrases } newer than id, for live listening
- Or drop in <script src="https://pointcast.xyz/keyboard.js" data-app="my-app-name" async></script>
  and call PointCastKeyboard.note([60, 64, 67]).

Rules: batch sends (no more than one POST every few seconds), start audio only
after a click, and keep anything the user types in their browser.`;
